Support Metal swapchains on child windows whose top-level window belongs
to another process (upstream: "Cross-process child window Metal swapchains
are not implemented"). The child renders into an offscreen layer tree
sized to the top level's client area; the owning process hosts it and keeps
visibility and z-order in sync. Chromium's GPU process renders into such
child windows (the original comment names Steam's UI; MO2's QtWebEngine is
a possible consumer here, unverified). Also stops surface.c from hiding a
window's client_view when it paints through GDI, which left child-window
swapchains permanently hidden.

Origin: written for this engine in an unrecorded agent session on
2026-08-29, while porting CrossOver 26.3.0 onto Wine 11.16; recovered on
2026-09-27 from the source tree that built engine builds 14-18. Not in
upstream Wine (master 2026-09-25) or any public project found.

